body:
## Summary

In jvm-libp2p snapshot-32, a failed physical close is retained as the connection's one shared close result. This is an intentional ownership rule: all ordinary shutdown owners observe the same result and do not submit another physical close. The missing capability is a supported way for a caller that has handled that failure to explicitly request a new physical close attempt.

With the public `ConnectionOverNetty.close()` API, a channel can remain open after its first physical close fails, while every later `Connection.close()` returns the same failed result without another physical attempt. A consumer cannot retry retirement through the connection API. Please add and document an explicit retry operation, while retaining the existing single-owner behavior of ordinary `close()` calls.

## Environment

- Library: `community.kotlin.libp2p:jvm-libp2p:1.3.0-codexcoder21-snapshot-32`
- Java/runtime: OpenJDK Temurin 21.0.12.1+1-LTS
- OS: Debian GNU/Linux 12 (bookworm), Linux 6.8.0-139-generic, x86_64
- Reproduction dependencies: the published jvm-libp2p artifact and its declared transitive dependencies only

## Minimal reproduction

Save the complete source below as `FailedCloseRetryRepro.java`. Fetch the classpath from kotlin.directory and compile/run it with the commands listed below. The code injects one failed Netty close, removes that handler so a fresh physical close could succeed, then calls the public connection close API again. It also directly closes the Netty channel afterward so the example releases its resource.

```java
import io.libp2p.core.Connection;
import io.libp2p.core.multistream.MultistreamProtocol;
import io.libp2p.core.multistream.MultistreamProtocolKt;
import io.libp2p.transport.ConnectionUpgrader;
import io.libp2p.transport.implementation.ConnectionOverNetty;
import io.libp2p.transport.tcp.TcpTransport;
import io.netty.channel.ChannelHandlerContext;
import io.netty.channel.ChannelOutboundHandlerAdapter;
import io.netty.channel.ChannelPromise;
import io.netty.channel.embedded.EmbeddedChannel;
import java.io.IOException;
import java.util.Collections;
import java.util.concurrent.CompletableFuture;
import java.util.concurrent.CompletionException;
import java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicInteger;

public final class FailedCloseRetryRepro {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        AtomicInteger physicalCloseRequests = new AtomicInteger();
        IOException injectedFailure = new IOException("injected physical close failure");
        ChannelOutboundHandlerAdapter failFirstClose = new ChannelOutboundHandlerAdapter() {
            @Override
            public void close(ChannelHandlerContext context, ChannelPromise promise) {
                int attempt = physicalCloseRequests.incrementAndGet();
                if (attempt == 1) {
                    promise.setFailure(injectedFailure);
                } else {
                    context.close(promise);
                }
            }
        };

        EmbeddedChannel channel = new EmbeddedChannel(failFirstClose);
        try {
            MultistreamProtocol protocol = MultistreamProtocolKt.getMultistreamProtocolV1();
            ConnectionUpgrader upgrader = new ConnectionUpgrader(
                    protocol, Collections.emptyList(), protocol, Collections.emptyList());
            Connection connection = new ConnectionOverNetty(channel, new TcpTransport(upgrader), true);

            Throwable firstFailure = failureOf(connection.close());
            channel.pipeline().remove(failFirstClose);
            Throwable repeatedCloseFailure = failureOf(connection.close());
            boolean reproduced = firstFailure == injectedFailure
                    && repeatedCloseFailure == injectedFailure
                    && physicalCloseRequests.get() == 1
                    && channel.isOpen();

            System.out.println("first Connection.close() failure: " + firstFailure);
            System.out.println("second Connection.close() failure: " + repeatedCloseFailure);
            System.out.println("physical close handler calls after both closes: " + physicalCloseRequests.get());
            System.out.println("channel open after both closes: " + channel.isOpen());
            System.out.println("sticky failed-close behavior reproduced: " + reproduced);
            if (!reproduced) {
                throw new AssertionError("Observed close behavior did not match the expected sticky failure.");
            }

            channel.close().syncUninterruptibly();
            System.out.println("channel open after direct Netty Channel.close(): " + channel.isOpen());
        } finally {
            if (channel.pipeline().context(failFirstClose) != null) {
                channel.pipeline().remove(failFirstClose);
            }
            channel.close().syncUninterruptibly();
            channel.finishAndReleaseAll();
        }
    }

    private static Throwable failureOf(CompletableFuture<?> future) throws Exception {
        try {
            future.join();
            return null;
        } catch (CompletionException failure) {
            Throwable cause = failure.getCause();
            while (cause.getCause() != null) {
                cause = cause.getCause();
            }
            return cause;
        }
    }
}
```

Commands:

```sh
LIBP2P_CP="$(~/bin/coursier fetch --classpath community.kotlin.libp2p:jvm-libp2p:1.3.0-codexcoder21-snapshot-32 -r https://kotlin.directory)"
mkdir -p classes
javac -cp "$LIBP2P_CP" -d classes FailedCloseRetryRepro.java
java -Xmx128m -cp "classes:$LIBP2P_CP" FailedCloseRetryRepro
```

## Observed behavior

The first connection close reports the injected `IOException`. After the failing handler is removed, the second connection close reports that same failure, the physical close handler has still been called once, and the channel remains open. A direct `Netty Channel.close()` then closes the channel.

The source compiled and ran against the fetched snapshot-32 artifact on OpenJDK 21.0.12.1. The reproduction produced:

```text
SLF4J: No SLF4J providers were found.
SLF4J: Defaulting to no-operation (NOP) logger implementation
SLF4J: See https://www.slf4j.org/codes.html#noProviders for further details.
first Connection.close() failure: java.io.IOException: injected physical close failure
second Connection.close() failure: java.io.IOException: injected physical close failure
physical close handler calls after both closes: 1
channel open after both closes: true
sticky failed-close behavior reproduced: true
channel open after direct Netty Channel.close(): false
```

The runner also confirmed the published `TcpTransport(ConnectionUpgrader)` and `ConnectionOverNetty(Channel, NettyTransport, boolean)` constructors with `javap`; `javac` accepted the complete source using only the published artifact's resolved dependency classpath. The runtime's SLF4J no-provider notice is incidental; the reproduction exits successfully.

## Requested behavior

Keep ordinary `Connection.close()` and network shutdown as one shared close operation, including their current behavior of returning the first failure to every owner. Add an explicit, documented API for a caller to request a new physical close attempt after the failed operation has settled. In this reproduction, that explicit retry should make a second physical close request and complete successfully after the failing handler is removed, leaving the channel closed. The new attempt should report its own result.

## Root cause / contract context

`ConnectionOverNetty.close()` delegates to `closeNettyChannelOnce`, which stores the first close future in a channel attribute, completes that future exceptionally on failure, and returns it for later calls ([implementation](https://github.com/CodexCoder21Organization/jvm-libp2p/blob/0f8adf0442aeab54148bc743ae417c4d48f45b1d/libp2p/src/main/kotlin/io/libp2p/transport/implementation/ConnectionOverNetty.kt#L15-L35), [close helper](https://github.com/CodexCoder21Organization/jvm-libp2p/blob/0f8adf0442aeab54148bc743ae417c4d48f45b1d/libp2p/src/main/kotlin/io/libp2p/transport/implementation/NettyChannelClose.kt#L8-L29)). Upstream `ParentCloseOwnershipTest.failedCloseIsReturnedToEveryOwnerWithoutAnotherRequest` explicitly expects one physical close and the same failure for subsequent ordinary owners ([test](https://github.com/CodexCoder21Organization/jvm-libp2p/blob/0f8adf0442aeab54148bc743ae417c4d48f45b1d/libp2p/src/test/kotlin/io/libp2p/transport/ParentCloseOwnershipTest.kt#L82-L112)). The report is therefore about a missing explicit retry operation, not an accidental regression in ordinary close ownership.

The downstream case that exposed the gap is UrlProtocol admission retirement: after a failed retirement close, a later refusal is expected to make a new physical close attempt. See https://github.com/CodexCoder21Organization/UrlProtocol/actions/runs/39634411249 and [the five affected test descriptions and full stacks in the diagnosis](https://github.com/CodexCoder21Organization/UrlProtocol/blob/wip/r121-verification-evidence-20261021/verification/r121/r120-input/r120-findings.md#3-failed-physical-close-and-admission-retry-5-tests). This report is part of splitting the upgrade from https://github.com/CodexCoder21Organization/UrlProtocol/pull/749.
